            "system_name": "Red Hat Bugzilla ID",
            "text": "2501535"
          }
        ],
        "notes": [
          {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "A flaw was found in CoreDNS. A remote attacker can send a specially crafted 28-byte UDP datagram to a CoreDNS server with the proxyproto plugin enabled. This malformed datagram can cause the CoreDNS process to crash, leading to a denial of service (DoS). The vulnerability arises from improper handling of a PROXY v2 header with a non-UDP transport type, which results in a nil pointer dereference.",
            "title": "Vulnerability description"
          },
          {
            "category": "summary",
            "text": "github.com/coredns/coredns: CoreDNS: Denial of Service via crafted UDP datagram with proxyproto plugin",
            "title": "Vulnerability summary"
          },
          {
            "category": "other",
            "text": "This vulnerability is rated as Important because a remote unauthenticated attacker can trigger a denial of service in CoreDNS by sending a specially crafted UDP datagram. This occurs when the `proxyproto` plugin is enabled, leading to a process crash. Red Hat products utilizing CoreDNS with this plugin enabled are susceptible to service disruption.",
            "title": "Statement"
          },
          {
            "category": "general",
            "text": "The CVSS score(s) listed for this vulnerability do not reflect the associated product's status, and are included for informational purposes to better understand the severity of this vulnerability.",
            "title": "CVSS score applicability"
          }
        ],
