            "system_name": "Red Hat Bugzilla ID",
            "text": "2520949"
          }
        ],
        "notes": [
          {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "A flaw was found in Micrometer's StatsD and Logging meter registries. This vulnerability allows a remote attacker to inject line terminators into metric data, such as names or tag values, due to insufficient sanitization of untrusted input. Exploitation can lead to the spoofing of arbitrary metrics, including critical system or business metrics, and the injection of false log entries, potentially impacting monitoring and auditing systems.",
            "title": "Vulnerability description"
          },
          {
            "category": "summary",
            "text": "io.micrometer/micrometer-registry-statsd: io.micrometer/micrometer-core: Micrometer: Line-protocol and log injection via unsanitized input allows metric and log spoofing",
            "title": "Vulnerability summary"
          },
