        "notes": [
          {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "A flaw was found in PostCSS. A remote attacker can exploit this vulnerability by providing a specially crafted sourceMappingURL when a specific configuration (the 'from' parameter) is not set. This can cause the application to read and expose unintended source-map files, potentially revealing sensitive information about the application's source code.",
            "title": "Vulnerability description"
          },
          {
            "category": "summary",
            "text": "postcss: PostCSS: Information disclosure via crafted sourceMappingURL",
            "title": "Vulnerability summary"
          },
          {
            "category": "other",
            "text": "Red Hat rates this flaw as Moderate because the information disclosed is limited to files with a .map extension. Source map files may contain source code paths and content, but the attacker cannot read arbitrary files on the system. Exploitation requires the application to process attacker-controlled CSS through PostCSS on the server side.",
            "title": "Statement"
          },
          {
            "category": "general",
            "text": "The CVSS score(s) listed for this vulnerability do not reflect the associated product's status, and are included for informational purposes to better understand the severity of this vulnerability.",
